// expect-error-at: 5348:17
mod:list_ptr_through_param;
// A POINTER PARAMETER HANDED ON IS THE ADDRESS OF ITS POINTEE (DEF-584, landing 177d2b3). `list_ptr_from_call.npk` freezes what holds a `List` while a pointer a call
// returned from `@h` is live. Here the callee is handed a pointer PARAMETER `hp`, which has no target in this frame: what the call may give back is what `@(<-hp)`
// would, so the same two questions are asked of the parameter's pointee type (`passed_pointee`, alias.npk), and where the value was READ out of the parameter
// (`hp.lp`, `<-hpp`, `hp[0i64]`) of the type it was read as (`ViewRef.read`, escape.npk's `mark_read_as`). THE YARDSTICK: a parameter form is refused wherever its
// local twin is (`@h` for `hp`; the twin's name has `l` after the number). Each module is one cell, each site NITPICK-BORROW-015.
//   THE HOLDER: `xb1` (the struct's `List` grown), `xb2` (a `List<int64>->` parameter), `xb3` (the `List` replaced), `xb6` (the field replaced), `xb7` (an aggregate
//     holder), and the explicit spellings refused before this row, `xb8` (`@(<-lp)[0i64]`) and `xb9` (`@hp.l[0i64]`).
//   THE TEMPORARY, live to the end of its full expression: `xb4`, `xn4` (through a copy), `xn5` (nested), `xq5` (a pointer member), `xk6` (inside a `dyn`), `xr9`
//     (the growth in a later argument's arm).
//   THE TARGET of an assignment, frozen whole while its value runs: `xb5`, `xk1`, `xk2`, `xk3`.
//   HOW THE PARAMETER REACHES THE CALL: nested in another call (`xn1`), copied to a local first (`xn2`), under a ternary (`xn3`), through a call that hands it back
//     (`xu1`; `xu2` and `xu5` with the growth in a callee), through a pointer to a copy of it (`xu4`), in a struct read whole through a pointer to the struct (`xp2`), as a
//     by-value struct parameter's member (`xo2`), as a method's `Self->` (`xo3`), as a receiver (`xm6b`, `xm13`), in a value a call built (`xm15`).
//   A HOLDER ASSIGNED LATER: `xh1`, `xh2` (in an inner block), `xh3` (in a loop), `xh4` (a field of it).
//   A VALUE READ OUT OF THE PARAMETER, judged by the type it was read as: a pointer member (`xm9`), a pointer to a pointer (`xm10`), an element of an array of
//     pointers (`xq3`) and of a `List` of them (`xq4`), each through a copy (`xq11`, `xq12`, `xq14`, `xq15`), the pointee stored whole (`xq16`, `xq17`) or its `List`
//     replaced (`xq18`). ONE NAME READ TWO WAYS keeps both refs: `xm12`, `xm12b`, `xm14`, `xt1` to `xt7`, `xd4`, and in a by-value parameter's own chain `xd5`, `xd6`.
//   THE POINTEE'S REACH is DEF-575's gate (`type_heap_holds`): an `any` member (`xg2`), a `dyn` (`xg4`, `xg5`), an enum holding the pointer (`xo5b`), a generic's
//     `T->` parameter at a struct beside its concrete twin (`xT5`, `xT5t`).
//   THE PRICES, right programs refused as their twins are: a sibling written while the pointer is live (`xs1` to `xs5`, `xq10`, `xk4`), a holder assigned after the
//     growth (`xh1c`), a generic's `T` holder (`xo6`), the element read before the growth with its holder still in scope (`xu1c`, `xg4c`, `xT3c`). ONE IS THIS
//     ROW'S OWN, `xpr1`: an `any->` parameter cast to a typed pointer and held across a write through another cast copy. It was `sfn_view_block_ended` in
//     `tests/backend/programs/param_copy_summary_ok.npk` until this landing; an `any->`'s pointee is anything, and its local twin `xpr1l` stays legal (the `_ok` file).
//   REFUSED BEFORE THIS ROW, the address spellings beside their parameter forms: `xm1` to `xm7`, `xr1` to `xr4`, `xh7c`, `xh8c`, `xp1`, and the in-place generic
//     at `T` = a struct (`xT3`, `xT3l`, `xT3t`, `xT4`, `xT4t`).
// STILL OPEN, in neither file: `kc8`'s family (a `List` behind a pointer member of what the callee was handed), DEF-323 (a holder with no initialiser), DEF-587
// (a parameter as the holder), DEF-590, DEF-591, DEF-592, and a `wild` slot's value, which asks nothing.
mod:xb1_param_struct_holder_grow = {
error:E5_xb1_param_struct_holder_grow;
struct:H = { List<int64>:l; int64:k; };
func:mk = List<int64>() never fails { List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(1i64); drop list_push(@l, 1i64); pass l; };
func:mkh = H() never fails { pass H{ l: raw mk(), k: 2i64 }; };
func:grow = int64(List<int64>->:p) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(p, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:growh = int64(H->:w) never fails { loop(0i64, 64i64, 1i64) { drop list_push(@w.l, 1i64); } pass 7i64; };
func:first = int64->(List<int64>->:q) never fails { pass @((<-q)[0i64]); };
func:fp = int64->(H->:q) never fails { pass @((<-q).l[0i64]); };
func:kp = int64->(H->:w) never fails { pass @w.k; };
func:getl = List<int64>->(H->:w) never fails { pass @w.l; };
func:idp = int64->(int64->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:rd2 = int64(int64->:e, int64:z) never fails { pass <-e; };
struct:PE = { int64->:p; int64:z; };
func:g = int64(H->:hp) never fails {
    int64->:e = raw fp(hp);
    discard(raw growh(hp));
    pass (<-e) + 6i64;
};
func:f = int64(int64:n) never fails {
    H:h = raw mkh();
    List<int64>:l = raw mk();
    pass raw g(@h);
};
};
